                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>This dataset contains the metadata of the three datasets used in the research study \"The effect of a general versus narrow undergraduate curriculum on graduate specialization: The case of a Dutch liberal arts college\" (DOI: 10.1002/curj.158).</p>\n\n<p>The datasets include academic performance and personal background data of two groups of students enrolled in three MSc programmes at Maastricht University:</p>\n\n<p>Dataset 1: International Business at the SBE;<br>\nDataset 2: Psychology at FPN;<br>\nDataset 3: Research Master in Cognitive and Clinical Neuroscience at FPN.</p>\n\n<p>The data included in these three datasets is as follows:<br>\n- Type of undergraduate education (1 = UCM degree; 0 = specialized bachelor's);<br>\n- Dropout status (1 = dropped out; 0 = graduated);<br>\n- Master GPA (10-point scale);<br>\n- Thesis grade (10-point scale);<br>\n- Bachelor GPA (10-point scale);<br>\n- Duration of master's studies (in years);<br>\n- Age (at the time of first registration);<br>\n- Gender (1 = female; 0 = male);<br>\n- Academic semester of first enrolment (1 = February; 0 = September)*;<br>\n- Academic year of first enrolment;<br>\n- Specialization track;<br>\n- Type of specialization track (1 = narrow/basic science tracks; 0 = broad/more applied tracks)**.</p>\n\n<p>* only included in Dataset 1<br>\n** only included in Dataset 1 and Dataset 2</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
